ow large the formula is.\n- **Against CooperateBot:** All three atoms are always true. From world 1 onward, X's action is therefore fixed by the values of those box bodies at (1,1,1). X defects against CooperateBot only if that value is D.\n- **Against FairBot at world 1:** A box at world 1 only looks at world 0. There, FairBot's atoms are also (1,1,1): FairBot's cooperation with X is vacuously true, it cooperates with CooperateBot, and □⊥ is true at world 0. So X plays D against FairBot at world 1.\n- **FairBot's reply:** FairBot's action at each world is the conjunction of X's earlier actions. That includes X's D at world 1, so FairBot defects from world 2 on.\n- **Conclusion:** No depth-1 agent can both defect against CooperateBot and be cooperated with by FairBot. The argument also covers depth 0 and never uses the DefectBot or self-play conditions.\n\nOn part 3, I did not characterize all depth-2 prudent agents or prove the formula minimal in size. `answer.md` gives only the structural reason depth 2 is needed: the agent must tell FairBot and CooperateBot apart at some world of 2 or later.","ttft_ms":2675,"type":"result","duration_ms":50962,"uuid":"3674b3c0-ce88-4f1c-a814-630f247a1e17","ttft_stream_ms":2490,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":2491,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":5428,"cacheReadInputTokens":87813,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12061,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0932338,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2866,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
